{"title":"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(with_minimal_trig)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (with minimal trig)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(tangent_half_angle)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (tangent half angle)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(if_you_forgot_angle_bisector_but_remember_LoS)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (if you forgot angle bisector but remember LoS)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Power Solve</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A circle centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> has radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and contains the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. The segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is tangent to the circle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/b/40bb7d97e256f7863394c099bf086e692619bfb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AOB = \\theta$\" width=\"88\" height=\"13\" />. If point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/c/37ca7a38f7eed488e5f646482c71b0cf56222e28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{OA}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> bisects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/bac8482f0d3f437f72c00e2f1bf7f7978944c158.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABO$\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/b/b0b0c876b9ad9b67c737661de98e24402a8e674a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OC =$\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/4/ea4f1560825547734d756bfe3b5548e6d92a8681.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import olympiad; size(6cm); unitsize(1cm); defaultpen(fontsize(8pt)+linewidth(.8pt)); labelmargin=0.2; dotfactor=3; pair O=(0,0); pair A=(1,0); pair B=(1,1.5); pair D=bisectorpoint(A,B,O); pair C=extension(B,D,O,A); draw(Circle(O,1)); draw(O--A--B--cycle); draw(B--C); label(&quot;$O$&quot;,O,SW); dot(O); label(&quot;$\\theta$&quot;,(0.1,0.05),ENE); dot(C); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,S); dot(A); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,E); dot(B); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,E);[/asy]\" width=\"112\" height=\"128\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/6/456f3281ffc32b835c0feb3c837932783f916aaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text {(A)}\\ \\sec^2 \\theta - \\tan \\theta \\qquad \\text {(B)}\\ \\frac 12 \\qquad \\text {(C)}\\ \\frac{\\cos^2 \\theta}{1 + \\sin \\theta}\\qquad \\text {(D)}\\ \\frac{1}{1+\\sin\\theta} \\qquad \\text {(E)}\\ \\frac{\\sin \\theta}{\\cos^2 \\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"590\" height=\"40\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is tangent to the circle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/c/dfc13f0783d8b0092bce37b79f5696127bec4586.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OAB$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is a right triangle. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/9/9d9c5fdf60b1981f939ac82b7a2b9eec2da963de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/0/97073bbbd2786991731205192436ace71cc46e82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = \\tan \\theta$\" width=\"90\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/0/8a05719b16dd9b8e091dd3ed7c49f3795912577b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OB = \\sec \\theta$\" width=\"88\" height=\"13\" />. By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle_Bisector_Theorem\" title=\"Angle Bisector Theorem\">Angle Bisector Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/7/69707027aaee20cd1affa3ab24e9df267be4e644.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{OB}{OC} = \\frac{AB}{AC} \\Longrightarrow AC \\sec \\theta = OC \\tan \\theta\\]\" width=\"287\" height=\"38\" /> We multiply both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/0/c7038458fdc92e1eb1840531bbb58b11dd5ba62e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\theta$\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" /> to simplify the trigonometric functions, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/feaa39c521fa4656bbfb421c013a3eb7498dfb68.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AC=OC \\sin \\theta\\]\" width=\"117\" height=\"13\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/1/fb1b9f872c5012dc29cf3c322fc6015f5bfb240c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC + OC = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"111\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/6/89625a83a890ebd2b3bd1d55ed2667f940ceae68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 - OC = OC \\sin \\theta \\Longrightarrow$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"184\" height=\"13\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/b/57b99dea1eeb8c239ec7a350c03bf7ae4d5d4692.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OC = \\dfrac{1}{1+\\sin \\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"121\" height=\"38\" />. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/e/37e78463fd8ed2f11d92cab9954c15a85484b595.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} \\dfrac{1}{1+\\sin \\theta}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"111\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Alternatively, one could notice that OC approaches the value 1/2 as theta gets close to 90 degrees.  The only choice that is consistent with this is (D).\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28with_minimal_trig.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(with_minimal_trig)\">Solution 3 (with minimal trig)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (with minimal trig)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let's assign a value to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> so we don't have to use trig functions to solve.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is a good value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, because then we have a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/0/8f040866096861a91f1b9c755be19cf0849ae480.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-60-90 \\triangle$\" width=\"114\" height=\"13\" /> -- <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/e/a7e94c6ac1760df1b4353f647bb2ad8ad52172ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC=90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"100\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is tangent to Circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Using our special right triangle, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/c/e0c972991a97a60dca2ed9721e6a1d083642c09d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/d/eade1bff13ace8fcb4deac440c1608e06f618aa9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OB=2$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/f/5cfe110024e4e993cceaa57a6acf6d170afcad84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/1/6a161754e13be8c23eaa38a2e52c58d9775a5cb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OC=x$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" />.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/1/e71c455ac42e8bb7ce3f5786424d823a0062f501.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA=1-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"93\" height=\"13\" />.  since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> bisects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/bac8482f0d3f437f72c00e2f1bf7f7978944c158.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABO$\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" />, we can use the angle bisector theorem:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/b/8ebe64d2124a7dfab83832c61f7c72457e0c0bdd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{x}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{1-x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"82\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/0/40032e6797ae0d48b38ebf64883cb8570b87ae74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2-2x=\\sqrt{3}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"109\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/5/79576145ca74c4c2b4edeae71f8086375e138495.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2=(\\sqrt{3}+2)x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/5/ab541558aea2903cbdd094d3ac328cda6e11fe1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"96\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>Now, we only have to use a bit of trig to guess and check: the only trig facts we need to know to finish the problem is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/5/955f3de541c807eb7bd0fdf23043c48ba2632204.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\theta =\\frac{\\text{Opposite}}{\\text{Hypotenuse}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"145\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/a/60a9b1165839c5406fe1404f37d1820082194259.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\theta =\\frac{\\text{Adjacent}}{\\text{Hypotenuse}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"147\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f4b2652c98ab49b2f572a211aefa331a496758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan\\theta =\\frac{\\text{Opposite}}{\\text{Adjacent}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"134\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>With a bit of guess and check, we get that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55bdade53f471aab49f63d1a734979cc0c636640.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"29\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/f/20f8f2f1a3ddc6b42fae25a0637e85c747875180.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OC$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> = x, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0964c9cf406ef8e5ec8beaa6a92125f2d8f90460.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> = h, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> = y. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a762ac8b4e23ffdd778ad6d5a8b97df8c7ce01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> - <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/f/20f8f2f1a3ddc6b42fae25a0637e85c747875180.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OC$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/f/20f8f2f1a3ddc6b42fae25a0637e85c747875180.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OC$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> = x, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a762ac8b4e23ffdd778ad6d5a8b97df8c7ce01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> = 1 (given in the problem), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> = 1-x.\n</p><p>Using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle_Bisector_Theorem\" title=\"Angle Bisector Theorem\">Angle Bisector Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3eafcc33911223f409f06caabac68b100230acbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{h}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"12\" height=\"41\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/4/7b4e1d98f4f934f03f1eae05aa6fade71d5203db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{1-x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"44\" height=\"33\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/1/981cc6a2adc50878a6da811d05c34e5cfaf6cef7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Longrightarrow$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"9\" /> h(1-x) = xy. Solving for x gives us x = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/6/cc66f7e09c099d0cadf5333ee533ae482c3ad33e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{h}{h+y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"44\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/b/3fb55686f6e0394320a1bc202589e98e5391cbf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\theta = \\frac{opposite}{hypotenuse} = \\frac{y}{h}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"190\" height=\"41\" />. Solving for y gives us y = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc612438a2fc32ac5393bc7e462c728a6f76408f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h \\sin\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Substituting this for y in our initial equation yields x = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/0/d30078f501b8cf2ef70dbed0eb455b6792e6ab1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{h}{h+h\\sin \\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"86\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>Using the distributive property, x = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/0/b207066f7dc77d8afd5ebea55c17eb47ca4ee9ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{h}{h(1+\\sin \\theta)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"92\" height=\"42\" /> and finally <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e735319c2fe91a24952523b792be4fd0de762037.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{1+\\sin \\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"68\" height=\"38\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/693c4044f8526a8179956e8ac7a3f2f9d61e2c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"43\" height=\"30\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is tangent to the circle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/5/7059791c8fd32a90dfd1f1b8ffddfbbb3b6b3c83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OAB=90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"104\" height=\"13\" /> and thus we can use trig ratios directly. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/a/a9aff7624fdaadd4307a3d0bd52348639fb865ae.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin{\\theta}=\\frac{\\overline{AB}}{\\overline{BO}}, \\cos{\\theta}=\\frac{1}{\\overline{BO}}, \\tan{\\theta}=\\overline{AB}\\]\" width=\"292\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>By the angle bisector theorem, we have \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/2/0a298ad91abb7dd31ea729f0e223734250ff2b64.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\overline{OB}}{\\overline{AB}}=\\frac{\\overline{OC}}{\\overline{CA}}\\]\" width=\"86\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Seeing the resemblance of the ratio on the left-hand side to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/d/6fd55dbd881a8b8e57758714905d3ff1ac329694.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{\\theta},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"38\" height=\"16\" /> we turn the ratio around to allow us to plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/6/d26625e0a0a6408e07999845e12a715d528c3952.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{\\theta}.$\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" /> Another source of motivation for this also lies in the idea of somehow adding 1 to the right-hand side so that we can substitute for a given value, i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/a/13a9d026ec240ce73e55f1decfb73c3da8df2186.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{OA}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" />, and flipping the fraction will preserve the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/1/0019a9c6ae9bef5eda9166daa34ea37465190dd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{OC}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" />, whilst adding one right now would make the equation remain in direct terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6f24388bacd8bfb276aa4219c1a9fd29abade05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CA}.$\" width=\"31\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/9/3294a4f30731279d9fe0d263ee2a857807b285b7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\overline{AB}}{\\overline{OB}}=\\sin{\\theta}=\\frac{\\overline{CA}}{\\overline{OC}}\\Rightarrow \\sin{\\theta}+1=\\frac{\\overline{CA}+\\overline{OC}}{\\overline{OC}}=\\frac{1}{\\overline{OC}}\\]\" width=\"403\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/84563b7341a82362643ab917230216c7b556bdde.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin{\\theta}+1=\\frac{1}{\\overline{OC}} \\Rightarrow \\boxed{\\overline{OC}=\\frac{1}{\\sin{\\theta}+1}}\\]\" width=\"284\" height=\"50\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28tangent_half_angle.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(tangent_half_angle)\">Solution 6 (tangent half angle)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (tangent half angle)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f93bc652aadfcdb353c6ace76a3d5cb77948d4f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CBO = 45^{\\circ} - \\frac{\\theta}{2}, \\angle ACB = 45^{\\circ} + \\frac{\\theta}{2}, OB = \\frac{1}{\\cos(\\theta)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"402\" height=\"42\" />.\nBy sine law, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/8/b087334c5e56b24e5331f8789978ac707c504887.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{OC}{\\sin(\\angle CBO)} = \\frac{OB}{\\sin(\\angle OCB)} = \\frac{OB}{\\sin(\\angle ACB)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"336\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/5/0751a954a2833fd23fd74c59c73535ba937b511e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[OC = \\frac{\\sin(45^{\\circ} - \\frac{\\theta}{2})}{\\sin(45^{\\circ} + \\frac{\\theta}{2})}OB = \\frac{\\sin(45^{\\circ} - \\frac{\\theta}{2})}{\\cos(45^{\\circ} - \\frac{\\theta}{2})}OB = \\tan(45^{\\circ} - \\frac{\\theta}{2})OB = \\frac{1-\\tan(\\theta/2)}{1+\\tan(\\theta/2)}OB\\]\" width=\"637\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/9/e6904ff57df9584b37003c163578212d8e959364.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = \\tan(\\theta/2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/5/c6533fc2e5dced8845a7d2f8fdde1f90bbeafc47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OC = \\frac{1-t}{1+t}OB = \\frac{1-t^2}{1+2t+t^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"233\" height=\"40\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/b/47b232695818cc0af7a26a16b900f72b99149903.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(\\theta) = \\frac{2t}{1+t^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"117\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/6/8d6db80c6cc6fa57bdb9296348b598083dd14688.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(\\theta) = \\frac{1-t^2}{1+t^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"119\" height=\"40\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/3/3631475aef5ad6ec09212aa9ca5455d2ea310c8b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[OC = \\frac{\\cos(\\theta)}{1+\\sin(\\theta)}OB = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} \\dfrac{1}{1+\\sin \\theta}}\\]\" width=\"297\" height=\"50\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7_.28if_you_forgot_angle_bisector_but_remember_LoS.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(if_you_forgot_angle_bisector_but_remember_LoS)\">Solution 7 (if you forgot angle bisector but remember LoS)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (if you forgot angle bisector but remember LoS)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/c/fbcc1caee8fe0b4f35fa182a81977616391d9f42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\overline{OC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/5/3350adbcfff02812bc823927ae9013edd09afb53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OBC=\\angle ABC=\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"174\" height=\"14\" />. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/a/6aa0ef1a11b0a3485f07f1fbf817c9f553d67128.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}=\\overline{OA}-\\overline{OC}=1-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"199\" height=\"19\" />. By the Law of Sines, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/1/231120ff65e5552e4af5606ffa78d6a4eba47bfb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{\\sin\\alpha}x=\\dfrac{\\sin\\theta}{BC}\\]\" width=\"100\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>and \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/a/73ac7034a8baef212421f4caea35bd214256337b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{\\sin\\alpha}{1-x}=\\dfrac{\\sin90^\\circ}{BC}=\\dfrac1{BC}.\\]\" width=\"183\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Combining the two give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/c/0dc7107ff24373418027c25dbe845837af0c9318.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\sin\\alpha}x=\\sin\\theta\\cdot\\dfrac{\\sin\\alpha}{1-x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"160\" height=\"40\" />. \n</p><p>Solving, this gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/b/4cb559b0c942f169e1d14d73139c46dd7ea52d07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{x=\\frac{1}{\\sin{\\theta}+1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"117\" height=\"51\" />. \n</p><p>~Technodoggo\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve\">Video Solution by Power Solve</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Power Solve\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J91b2g68oM0\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J91b2g68oM0</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/zGnRV6eNiV0\">https://youtu.be/zGnRV6eNiV0</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12\" title=\"2000 AMC 12\">2000 AMC 12</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Answer_Key\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" sty